title: '[RWF] sc-client-db: fix finalization can leave best_number below finalized_number'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: "Closes #12305.\n\n## Summary\n`finalize_block_with_transaction` always\
    \ returns `MetaUpdate { is_best: false, .. }`, and `update_meta` only updates\
    \ `best_number`/`best_hash` when `is_best` is true. If the best block is behind\
    \ the block being finalized (e.g. after a re-org moves `best` to an earlier block),\
    \ finalizing a later block leaves `best_number < finalized_number` \u2014 violating\
    \ the metadata invariant.\n\n## Fix\nIn `update_meta`, when applying a finalized\
    \ `MetaUpdate`, if `number > meta.best_number`, advance `best_number`/`best_hash`\
    \ to match. A finalized block is canonical by definition, so `best` can never\
    \ legitimately lag behind `finalized`."
crates:
- name: sc-client-db
  bump: patch
